HIGH LEVEL DESIGN (HLD) :
    This system is an end-to-end GenAI-powered AML (Anti-Money Laundering) risk detection platform designed to analyze financial transactions and classify risk using Multi-Agent architecture and RAG-based contextual reasoning.

    System Flow
        Transaction data is ingested into Databricks Lakehouse
        Data is processed through Bronze → Silver → Gold layers
        Gold layer is exposed to FastAPI inference service
        Orchestrator manages request flow
        Multi-Agent system processes request:
        Retriever Agent → fetches policy context using FAISS
        Reasoning Agent → generates explanation
        Validation Agent → applies AML rules
        Final response includes risk score, flags, and reasoning
    Architecture Layers
        Data Layer (Databricks Lakehouse)
        API Layer (FastAPI)
        Orchestration Layer
        Multi-Agent Layer
        RAG Layer (FAISS Vector DB)
        Security Layer (RBAC + Guardrails)
        LLMOps Layer (Logging + Monitoring)
LOW LEVEL DESIGN (LLD) :
    Databricks Pipeline
        Bronze: Raw ingestion of transactions
        Silver: Data cleaning, type casting, deduplication
        Gold: Risk scoring + feature enrichment
    RAG Pipeline
        Policy documents embedded using SentenceTransformer
        Stored in FAISS index
        Query → embedding → similarity search → top-k context retrieval
    Multi-Agent System
        Retriever Agent: Fetches relevant compliance policies
        Reasoner Agent: Generates AML explanation using context
        Validator Agent: Applies rule-based risk checks
    Risk Scoring Logic
        High amount (>10,000) → risk increase
        High-risk countries → risk increase
        Crypto/investment → risk increase
        High transaction frequency → risk increase
    Security Layer
        Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
        Prompt Injection Detection
        Sensitive Data Masking
        Audit Logging